\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces TRL architecture. Pipeline stages register typed relations among runs, evidence, claims, decisions and manuscript assertions. A revision event enters the transaction manager, which applies it to a private copy, propagates it through the lineage closure, checks invariants $I_1$--$I_8$, and either commits a content-addressed, hash-chained snapshot or rolls back. The export gate admits a manuscript only if every assertion is ledger-admissible under the registered graph.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{2}{TRL architecture. Pipeline stages register typed relations among runs, evidence, claims, decisions and manuscript assertions. A revision event enters the transaction manager, which applies it to a private copy, propagates it through the lineage closure, checks invariants $I_1$--$I_8$, and either commits a content-addressed, hash-chained snapshot or rolls back. The export gate admits a manuscript only if every assertion is ledger-admissible under the registered graph}{figure.1}{}}
